source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: A heading line is a line domain like any other, so Jira breaks inside the heading. A JFM ATX heading carries no hard break, so jiro keeps both backslashes as heading text and warns rather than writing a break that would read back as a character Jira never showed.
-- input.jira --
h1. a\\b
-- rendered.html --
<h1><a name="a%5C%5Cb"></a>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" />b</h1>
-- want.md --
# a\\\\b
-- warnings.json --
[
  {
    "Line": 1,
    "Column": 6,
    "Construct": "heading",
    "Reason": "Jira would render a forced newline inside this heading; a JFM heading cannot carry one, so the characters stay literal"
  }
]
